    "created_at": "2015-10-26T15:49:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-26T16:06:57Z",
    "body": "A more verbose description would be appreciated.\n\nYour hint: \"second parent is a variable\" doesn't help very much, is the first parent not a variable?\n\nConsidering: \"To replace a child with node within a parent, run these steps:\"\nThen: \"If child’s parent is not parent\"\n\nWe want to replace a child of a parent with some other node in an existing dom structure, so implying that child's parent is not parent would imply that this structure is not a valid one.\n\nEdit:\n\nFurther thinking about what this could mean I came to this conclusion:\n\nfunc replaceNode(targetDom, nodeToBeReplaced, newNode)\n\nwhere:\ntargetDom = parent\nnodeToBeReplaced = child\nnewNode = node\nchild's parent = child.parent\n\nin which we are expected to check if the provided nodeToBeReplaced (child) indeed is inside the targetDom(parent) structure.\n\nSeriously, I have shown this passage to 3 different people and no one was able to tell what this thing was about, but imho this should be the exact purpose of this document.\n\nAnd this is the Issue I am concerned about.\n",
